    "available_at": "2026-11-26T15:55:54.268441+00:00",
    "body": "Overhead view of the Media Luna operation in Mexico. Credit: Torex Resources.\nBy: Northern Miner Staff November 26, 2026\nTorex Resources (TSX, NYSE: TXR) is considering two mill upgrades at its Morelos complex in Mexico as part of a plan to nearly double output within five years, according to Red Cloud Securities.\nThe larger expansion would cost about $100 million (C$142.2 million) and lift processing capacity to 14,500 tonnes a day, Red Cloud mining analyst Ron Stewart said Thursday in a note. A construction decision is targeted for the first quarter of 2028.\nAn earlier $5-million to $10-million upgrade would remove processing bottlenecks and raise capacity by about 15% by the end of 2027, Torex’s latest earnings presentation shows.\nTorex’s Los Reyes gold-silver project in Sinaloa state would provide another source of growth. “Based on a preliminary project timeline, construction of Los Reyes would commence in 2029 with first production in 2031,” CEO Andrew Snowden said in July.\nRed Cloud’s Stewart sees a path to an annualized production rate of about 800,000 gold-equivalent oz. by the end of 2031, up from roughly 450,000 for now. The Morelos mine in Guerrero state could supply about 650,000 oz. of that total, with the remainder coming from Los Reyes.\nDecember start\nThe next milestone is Media Luna North, where Torex expects first ore before year-end, with Stewart anticipating a December start. The company forecasts an average mining rate of about 1,000 tonnes a day in 2027, with further increases toward its design capacity of about 2,300 tonnes a day.\nLos Reyes would require an initial $515 million, which Torex expects to fund from Morelos cash flow. The July preliminary economic assessment forecasts annual output averaging 161,000 gold-equivalent oz. during the first 11 years, comprising 111,000 oz. of gold and 3.6 million oz. of silver. The average falls to 134,000 gold-equivalent oz. over the full 14.4-year mine life as lower-grade stockpiles enter the mill. Torex plans a prefeasibility study in 2027 and a feasibility study in 2028.\nTorex shares dropped 0.2% to C$64.35 Thursday morning in Toronto, valuing the company at about C$5.8 billion ($4.1 billion). They have traded between C$51.40 and C$85 over the past year.\nPrint\nTAG: gold mines gold mining gold production gold projects Mexico mining silver production\nCOMMODITY: Gold Silver\nREGION: Canada Mexico and Central America\nCOMPANY: Torex Resources\nRepublish this article",
